  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Expanding on the current tag system for avatars to extend to worlds and be used for a visibility toggle for avatars.\nMake users opt-in to see any avatars tagged as NSFW, as well as allow World Creators and per-instance creation to tag whether NSFW tagged content is allowed within, by default these should be off. If a user does not opt-in or an NSFW avatar is loaded but the world/instance is not set to allow such, load a default fall back in place for the users not-opting in to see such. Avatars that are clearly NSFW without the tag should be reportable and blocked from use or force tagged, a warning could be given to the uploader as well. This would help prevent NSFW content from being seen in public spaces unwanted or being seen by minors. This system would not prevent minors from seeing NSFW content entirely, but would shift the responsibility of regulating it's visibility to the minor themselves or their guardian and not VRChat itself. The child would have to willingly and with intent opt-into the feature and if their guardian wishes to not let their child see such, it is their choice and within their power to keep them opted-out.\nThis entire system was thought up with NSFW control in mind, but could be expanded for accessibility or trauma related issues, by allowing more tags to be opt-in or chosen to block by the user, such as \"Violence\", \"Blood\", \"Flashing Lights\", etc... \nI hope this idea is plausible and can be considered in part. NSFW is a hard topic to develop around for the game, and will exist regardless of TOS enforcement. I hope a robust self-regulating system like this can at least make it so those who should not or wish to simply not see, can still avoid it, while those who for many reasons still want to see or participate in NSFW content (whether it be for long distance intimacy, hobby dancing sexual in nature, and many others) can do so without upset or discomfort.",
